Package: geochemR
Title: Import, Process and Map Geochemical Data (XRD, XRF, Pyrolysis)
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R:
    person("Matthew", "Jorden", , "matthew.jorden@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A tidy data model and toolkit for sample-based geochemistry from
    boreholes, wells and outcrops: X-ray diffraction mineralogy (XRD), X-ray
    fluorescence element and oxide chemistry (XRF), and source-rock analyzer /
    Rock-Eval pyrolysis (S1, S2, S3, Tmax, TOC). Readers turn wide laboratory
    spreadsheets into one validated long table with detection-limit handling;
    processing covers unit and oxide-element conversion, renormalisation,
    compositional (log-ratio) transforms and derived indices (HI, OI, PI,
    vitrinite-reflectance equivalent, chemical index of alteration,
    mineralogical brittleness); and plotting covers depth profiles, hole-by-depth
    heatmaps, interpolated cross-sections, planar maps with inverse-distance
    surfaces, ternary diagrams and kerogen-type plots, all as 'ggplot2' objects.
